@cc [owner:fabiencelier,label:product;mcp] changes-are-suggestions
Tools of the `building_agents_and_skills` MCP server MUST NOT modify an agent or a skill directly.
Every tool that proposes a change records a `pending` agent or skill suggestion with source `conversational` for the
editors to review, marks conflicting pending suggestions `outdated`, and returns the suggestion
`sId` embedded in a directive (`:agent_suggestion[]{sId=... kind=...}` or
`:skill_suggestion[]{sId=... kind=... skillId=...}`) so the conversation UI can render it inline.

@cc [owner:avervaet,label:product] agent-creation-suggestion-has-no-real-agent-yet
`suggest_agent_creation` records a `kind: "create"` `AgentSuggestion`, complying with
`changes-are-suggestions` above: it MUST NOT make the proposed agent usable. The suggestion's
`agentConfigurationId` points at a placeholder created by `createPendingAgentConfiguration`
(`status: "pending"`, `scope: "hidden"`, no actions, creator as sole editor) purely to give the
suggestion a stable, non-null foreign key — that placeholder MUST stay excluded from every agent
listing until a human reviews the suggestion and turns it into a real agent.
